ion has come the time to  review our ambitions upwards the new  Commission fully recognized fully  recognizes that boosting European  infrastructures including notably  broadband is key for digital growth our  economy in society so badly need as you  know President Juncker  had tasked vice-president catenin  at the very beginning of his mandate to  present proposal for 315 billion euro  package of private and public investment  within the next three years  this took form of the recently released  investment plan for Europe with this  strong focus on  structures including broadband we should  get a fair share of the package within a  framework of the pipeline building  exercise we have got from the member  states almost 500 proposals for ICT in  broad on projects covering a total  investment sum of more than 150 billion  euro over 2015 17 the main pillar of the  investment plan will be new European  funds for strategic investments to be  set up within the European Investment  Bank member states directly or fraud or  national promotional banks will have the  opportunity to contribute to the fund by  paying in capital a clear focus of the  investment package will be the support  to investment in ultra-fast networks as  you know our current targets for 2020  that you all so passionately criticize  are to have all EU citizens connected to  30 megabits per second and all of them  connected 200 megabits per second what  we are worried about is actually that  the second objective is at serious risk  of not being achieved within the time  frame at the same time there is a clear  demand for in-house high quality  personalized entertainment Ultra HD also  gaming as we have seen in the beginning  of this event a multi-screen and multi  device vision teleworking that was also  mentioned here and innovative SMEs  require guaranteed upload speeds we have  not yet assess the need for fixing  in our higher target like one gigabit  per second but we clearly see the  emergence of such